From: z5vix <z5vix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UWP Store: UWP Minecraft: window reuse, DeviceInformation FindAllAsync with kind, Media Foundation delay-load exports, Store product queries

Applies after 92-uwpstore-xbox-app-identity.patch. Found bringing UWP Minecraft (Microsoft.MinecraftUWP) from a crash on its first frame to its welcome screen:
- wineuwp: the window factory allows window reuse. Answering FALSE made twinapi.appcore create a second view
  for the launch activation, calling the app's IFrameworkViewSource::CreateView a second time. Minecraft moves
  its game factory into the first view it creates, so the view it was activated in had none and faulted on a
  NULL in its first tick. WINE_UWP_NO_WINDOW_REUSE gives the old answer. The Xbox app still reaches its main
  screen with reuse allowed.
- windows.devices.enumeration: IDeviceInformationStatics2::FindAllAsync (filter, properties, kind), sharing
  the Statics FindAllAsync path; kind picks the DevQuery object type as CreateFromIdAsync does. Its E_NOTIMPL
  became a winrt::hresult_not_implemented in Minecraft's start-up.
- mfplat: exports Windows.Media.dll, Windows.Media.Audio.dll and Windows.Media.Editing.dll delay-load
  (MFCreatePropertiesFromMediaType, MFCreateMediaTypeFromProperties, MFCreateTelemetrySession, ...), answering
  E_NOTIMPL. A missing export ended the process through the delay-load failure hook; a failed call is reported
  to the caller instead.
- windows.services.store: GetStoreProductsAsync and GetAssociatedStoreProductsAsync answer a completed query
  with no products (an empty, iterable IMapView<String, StoreProduct>; AddOnLicenses becomes iterable too).
  Minecraft asks for its add-on catalogue at start-up, and the E_NOTIMPL ended it as an unobserved task
  exception.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/dlls/wineuwp/main.c
+++ b/dlls/wineuwp/main.c
@@ -4693,11 +4693,16 @@
     return hr;
 }
 
+/* Whether the activation may land in the view the app already has. On Windows a launch of an app that is starting
+ * up goes to its main view; answering FALSE made twinapi.appcore create a second view, calling the app's
+ * IFrameworkViewSource::CreateView again. Minecraft (UWP) hands its game factory to the first view it creates, so
+ * the second view it was activated in had none and faulted on its first frame. WINE_UWP_NO_WINDOW_REUSE restores
+ * the old answer. */
 static HRESULT WINAPI wf_get_WindowReuseAllowed( struct window_factory *wf, boolean *value )
 {
     TRACE( "%p\n", value );
     if (!value) return E_POINTER;
-    *value = FALSE;
+    *value = !GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINE_UWP_NO_WINDOW_REUSE", NULL, 0 );
     return S_OK;
 }
 
